{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"CLSA-2026-1791914243","published":"2026-10-13T17:57:36Z","modified":"2026-10-26T09:43:51.707224401Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-42356","CVE-2026-48005","CVE-2026-63686","CVE-2026-63718","CVE-2026-73636","CVE-2026-73637"],"summary":"httpd: Fix of 6 CVEs","details":"- CVE-2026-42356: do not run the target of a CGI internal redirect with the\n  handler derived from the CGI request's trusted content type\n- CVE-2026-63686: fix mod_xml2enc NULL pointer dereference when a charset\n  conversion partially succeeds and then fails\n- CVE-2026-63718: fix mod_proxy_uwsgi response smuggling via backend\n  Transfer-Encoding by dropping hop-by-hop response headers\n- CVE-2026-73636: fix mod_auth_digest one-time nonce replay\n- CVE-2026-73637: fix mod_auth_digest use-after-free of shared client entries\n  on concurrent requests\n- CVE-2026-48005: fix mod_auth_digest forced re-authentication via forged\n  Authorization headers with AuthDigestNcCheck\n- mod_auth_digest: configs using \"AuthDigestQop none\" or the \"authdigest-opaque\"\n  Mutex type no longer start (the shipped manual still documents\n  \"AuthDigestQop none\"); RFC 2069 clients (no qop) are refused; with\n  AuthDigestNcCheck On or AuthDigestNonceLifetime 0, 503 if no client entry\n  fits in shared memory; log ids AH01767, AH01771, AH01772, AH01792 and\n  AH01793 are removed\n- mod_auth_digest: with AuthDigestNcCheck On, a request that is authenticated\n  twice (e.g. a DirectoryIndex file in its own <Files> section) is refused\n  with 401\n- mod_auth_digest: after a reload (also the logrotate one) or a SIGHUP restart\n  a captured request can be accepted once more under AuthDigestNonceLifetime 0\n  or AuthDigestNcCheck; only stopping httpd (systemctl restart) invalidates\n  it (fixed upstream only in trunk f4c4160fbf, not in 2.4.69)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"httpd","ecosystem":"TuxCare:CentOS-Stream:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/httpd?distro=centos-stream-8"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM"